<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9529" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">com-parco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conp-</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comperco</span></b> 
				(<i><span class="en">Sol. 22, 17</span></i>), parsi or
			persi, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to save</i>, <i>husband
			well</i>, <i>lay up</i> (ante- and post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quod ille compersit miser,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 1, 1, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cibum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fronto, Laud. Neglig. 2, p. 371</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Pacat. Pan. Theod. 32 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to abstain</i>, <i>forbear;</i> with <i>inf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conperce, amabo, me attrectare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 2, 137</span></i>
			; cf. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 60, 5</span></i>
		Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
